      "text": "1) How to guarantee an accept notification is never dropped?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1) How to guarantee an accept notification is never dropped?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "oCGEDY3Yz8XKxk9-xpFn1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1044.8147883098914,
      "y": 1085.5073695693488,
      "width": 1364.977163978925,
      "height": 275,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "buu",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 226653908,
      "version": 370,
      "versionNonce": 2052479700,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786847368137,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Publish notification first to durable queue, if crash before, the enqueue caller gets errors and send again.\n- Delivery work like this:\n\n1) A worker receives a message from the queue, which hides it from other workers for a visibility timeout.\n2) It looks up the recipient's email address or device token and checks their preferences.\n3) It calls the provider.\n4) It writes the outcome to a Notification row in Postgres, SENT if the provider accepted it and FAILED if it didn't. \nA FAILED row records the attempt and leaves the message eligible for retry.\n5) Only then does it delete the message from the queue.\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Publish notification first to durable queue, if crash before, the enqueue caller gets errors and send again.\n- Delivery work like this:\n\n1) A worker receives a message from the queue, which hides it from other workers for a visibility timeout.\n2) It looks up the recipient's email address or device token and checks their preferences.\n3) It calls the provider.\n4) It writes the outcome to a Notification row in Postgres, SENT if the provider accepted it and FAILED if it didn't. \nA FAILED row records the attempt and leaves the message eligible for retry.\n5) Only then does it delete the message from the queue.\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
