      "y": 1808.3766158361314,
      "width": 812.1290421378342,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bv1",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2019278956,
      "version": 714,
      "versionNonce": 1790049108,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786853332032,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1) Circuit breaker: track failure and timeout rate per provider, once it cross\nthreshold,\nbreaker opens, call fail immediately instead of wait for timeout, so we can shed\nnon-essential load and leave room for high priority\n2) Bulkhead: cap # of calls one provider can be in flight at once. Once it pass\nthreshold, no more workers start call to it, so we not spinning capacity on down\nservices\n3) Provider router: channels that have backup for primary.  eg: if SMS is down, can\nroute to email (and need to plan if email service suddenly overload)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1) Circuit breaker: track failure and timeout rate per provider, once it cross threshold,\nbreaker opens, call fail immediately instead of wait for timeout, so we can shed\nnon-essential load and leave room for high priority\n2) Bulkhead: cap # of calls one provider can be in flight at once. Once it pass threshold, no more workers start call to it, so we not spinning capacity on down services\n3) Provider router: channels that have backup for primary.  eg: if SMS is down, can route to email (and need to plan if email service suddenly overload)",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "efB_f2PjGcpQ5W9ROPjJ6",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1046.9865025600855,
