    {
      "id": "MvlEe9g19NEz3wKwnIkpI",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1055.968009077222,
      "y": 2110.280038110223,
      "width": 938.486433518397,
      "height": 475,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bv5",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 176720212,
      "version": 459,
      "versionNonce": 1151412692,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786853846246,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Eg: pull notification off queue, worker call Twillio but dies before it delete message, message\nsent but queue has not been deleted \n- Solution: check before the SEND, Record after the ACK\n- The fix is to flip the order. We can check whether we've already sent it before dispatching,\nand write the dedup marker only after the provider has taken it.\n- Check DB before each notification can be slow, so use REDIS as cache of recently sent IDs\n\nGET sent:{notificationId}              # before dispatch: present -> duplicate, drop it\nSET sent:{notificationId} 1 EX 172800  # only after the provider accepts (48h covers DLQ\nreplays)\n\n- worker grabs a notification, it first checks Redis to see if it was already sent. If yes, drop\nit and grab the next one. If no, send it, update the DB, and update the cache.\n\n\n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Eg: pull notification off queue, worker call Twillio but dies before it delete message, message\nsent but queue has not been deleted \n- Solution: check before the SEND, Record after the ACK\n- The fix is to flip the order. We can check whether we've already sent it before dispatching, and write the dedup marker only after the provider has taken it.\n- Check DB before each notification can be slow, so use REDIS as cache of recently sent IDs\n\nGET sent:{notificationId}              # before dispatch: present -> duplicate, drop it\nSET sent:{notificationId} 1 EX 172800  # only after the provider accepts (48h covers DLQ replays)\n\n- worker grabs a notification, it first checks Redis to see if it was already sent. If yes, drop it and grab the next one. If no, send it, update the DB, and update the cache.\n\n\n\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
